; ============================================================================
; BSYS_BarterCloseUDE
; ============================================================================
; Close handler for barter (1053) and dialogue (1009). Closing BARTER with
; a fence offers the intel list - but only as DISCOVERY (some row never
; brought up before; see BSYS_IntelListUDF's bChain 0 rule).
;
; DELIBERATELY does nothing on dialogue close: menu open/close order
; across the dialogue<->barter swap is untrustworthy in BOTH directions
; (log-proven), so a close-side capture clear could clobber the partner
; mid-conversation and silently kill the list. Every consumer runs after
; a recapturing menu-open, and GameScript releases all conversation state
; (capture + greeting claim) once no menu has been open for 2 frames.
; ============================================================================

Create: BSYS_BarterCloseUDE

int iMenuId

Begin Function { iMenuId }
  if iMenuId == 1053
    Call BSYS_IntelListUDF 0
  endif
End
